Hi @DTekNOdev, thanks for the submission! 👋

One issue to fix before this can be added: the card renders alert fields that come from external feeds (USGS/NWS/RSS, per the README) directly into the DOM without escaping. In `_renderAlert` (and `_renderDismissedAlert`), the values `${alert.title}`, `${alert.message}`, `${alert.area}`, and `${alert.instruction}` are interpolated straight into `this.shadowRoot.innerHTML`. Because that text comes from third-party feeds, a feed item whose title or message contains markup like `<img src=x onerror=...>` would execute script in the Home Assistant frontend.

Please escape those feed-derived values before inserting them (for example, render them via `textContent`, or run them through an HTML-escape helper) so untrusted feed content can't inject markup. Once that's in place, cut a new release and re-request review.

