Thanks for this one, Colin. Approved and merging.

One non-blocking note for whenever you next touch the README. The troubleshooting line "Certificate, connection and reload sensors are unavailable" describes something the code does not do: when no metrics address is set, those `value_fn` callables return `None`, so the entities stay available and report unknown. Your own comment above `open_connections` says exactly that ("stays unknown unless one was configured"), and the "Backend unhealthy" section spells out the same reasoning for the binary sensor. Only that one troubleshooting line is out of step. The router line just below it is correct, because `TraefikRouterEntity.available` really does go false when a router drops out of the configuration.

